      lead: 'C2PA is an open technical standard, published by the Coalition for Content Provenance and Authenticity, for recording how a piece of media was made and attaching that record to the file with a cryptographic signature. When you see the name Content Credentials in an Adobe, OpenAI or Google product, that is C2PA under a friendlier label. Its value is specific and worth stating precisely: it does not detect AI, it carries a claim that can be verified or shown to have been broken.',
