      insights: [
        {
          heading: 'Why generation parameters live outside EXIF',
          body: 'EXIF was designed for cameras: fixed tags for exposure, aperture, ISO and lens. A prompt, a seed and a serialised node graph do not fit that shape, so the Stable Diffusion ecosystem writes them into PNG text chunks instead, which accept arbitrary key/value strings. This is the single most common misunderstanding in the area — searches for "ComfyUI EXIF" or "PNG info" are almost always looking for text chunks, not camera tags. The practical upshot is that you need a reader that inspects both regions, because a tool that only parses EXIF will report an empty result on a file that is full of readable evidence.',
